      "total_response_seconds": 8.0391,
      "response": "*The Arab Tent* is a fascinating oil painting by Edwin Landseer, dating from around 1865 to 1866. It's a rare example of Landseer engaging with the \"Orientalist\" themes that were very fashionable at the time.\n\nIf you look closely, you'll see an Arab mare and her foal, along with two Persian greyhounds and two monkeys\u2014one of whom is even wearing an earring! Interestingly, the artist arranged it so that the animals become more intelligent the higher up the picture you look. While the owner isn't visible, their presence is suggested by two pipes sitting in a jar on the right.\n\nIt's also one of the most expensive artworks bought by the founders of the collection; Sir Richard Wallace purchased it from the Prince of Wales for the substantial sum of \u00a36,300.",
